    <item>
      <title>From: Craig and Carmen Ramsay, To: Ruby Chandler Mulholland</title>
      <link>//localhost:1313/1927/11/15/635/</link>
      <pubDate>Tue, 15 Nov 1927 00:53:34 +0000</pubDate>
      <guid>//localhost:1313/1927/11/15/635/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;//localhost:1313/wp-content/uploads/2014/05/postcard-2014-20140507_18540868_0227.jpg&#34;&gt;&lt;img alt=&#34;postcard-2014-20140507_18540868_0227&#34; loading=&#34;lazy&#34; src=&#34;//localhost:1313/wp-content/uploads/2014/05/postcard-2014-20140507_18540868_0227.jpg&#34;&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;//localhost:1313/wp-content/uploads/1927/11/postcard-2014-20140528_18255275_0382.jpg&#34;&gt;&lt;img alt=&#34;postcard-2014-20140528_18255275_0382&#34; loading=&#34;lazy&#34; src=&#34;//localhost:1313/wp-content/uploads/1927/11/postcard-2014-20140528_18255275_0382.jpg&#34;&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;From: Craig and Carmen Ramsay, To: Sam Mulholland&lt;br&gt;
Mailed From: Kansas on November 15, 1927&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Mrs. Sam Mulholland&lt;br&gt;
Pearl, Illinois&lt;br&gt;
c/o Mrs. Chandler&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Dear Mrs. Mulholland,&lt;br&gt;
May I express my most sincere sympathy to you and your family in your bereavement. I know only too well what you are going through. I only wish I could do something to brighten your sorrow.&lt;br&gt;
Sincerely,&lt;br&gt;
Craig and Carmen Ramsay&lt;/p&gt;</description>
